On Tue, 14 Jul 2026 at 13:22, Elena Vasquez <elena.vasquez@acme-robotics.example> wrote:
> Jack,
>
> Marcus asked me to run the security review for the Reno pilot. Before I schedule anything I want to flag a concern up front so nobody is surprised later.
>
> Your trust page says YAGNI holds a SOC 2 Type I report. Our vendor policy requires SOC 2 Type II for any software that runs on a network segment with access to production systems, and the edge agent would sit on the Reno floor network next to Fulcrum and the AMR fleet manager. A Type I tells me your controls were designed sensibly on one day; it does not tell me they operated for six months. That is a real gap for us, and I can't waive it on my own authority.
>
> To start the review, can you send me your current SOC 2 report and the summary of your most recent external penetration test? I'll also need your subprocessor list and a data-flow diagram for the agent eventually, but the first two are what I need now.
>
> I'd rather find a path than block this, but I need to be clear that the Type II question will come back at the end.
>
> Elena
